689 0 obj
<<
/Title (RESEARCH METHODOLOGY Script This study uses a Developmental Research Design to develop and evaluate the proposed system.)
/Dest [25 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 691 0 R
/Next 687 0 R
>>
endobj
690 0 obj
<<
/Title (CONCEPTUAL FRAMEWORK Script This slide presents the conceptual framework of the study. The inputs consist of stress level, academic workload, sleep hours, and study time.)
/Dest [22 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 688 0 R
/Next 692 0 R
>>
endobj
691 0 obj
<<
/Title (Furthermore, the study contributes to educational monitoring and serves as a reference for future AI-based burnout research.)
/Dest [24 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 693 0 R
/Next 689 0 R
>>
endobj
692 0 obj
<<
/Title (These variables undergo preprocessing, MFBI computation, and Machine Learning analysis to generate burnout classification and early warning notifications.)
/Dest [22 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 690 0 R
/Next 694 0 R
>>
endobj
693 0 obj
<<
/Title (It also assists teachers and guidance counselors in monitoring students who may be vulnerable to burnout.)
/Dest [24 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 695 0 R
/Next 691 0 R
>>
endobj
694 0 obj
<<
/Title (SCOPE AND LIMITATION Script The study focuses on selected college students in Lanao del Norte.)
/Dest [23 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 692 0 R
/Next 696 0 R
>>
endobj
695 0 obj
<<
/Title (SIGNIFICANCE OF THE STUDY Script The study benefits students by promoting burnout awareness and early intervention.)
/Dest [24 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 697 0 R
/Next 693 0 R
>>
endobj
696 0 obj
<<
/Title (It utilizes stress level, workload, sleep hours, and study time as predictors of burnout and applies Random Forest and Decision Tree algorithms for analysis.)
/Dest [23 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 694 0 R
/Next 697 0 R
>>
endobj
697 0 obj
<<
/Title (The system is intended solely for burnout monitoring, prediction, and early warning and is not designed for clinical diagnosis.)
/Dest [23 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 696 0 R
/Next 695 0 R
>>
